{%- comment -%}
  ============================================================================
  PD TREATMENT — THOMPSON SAMPLING (real scoring, wired live)
  ============================================================================
  App embed block: injects assets/pd-treatment.js on every storefront page.
  The script asks /apps/pd/assign (the app proxy) which arm
  (control/treatment) the visitor is in for the collection they're viewing
  (using the SAME assignment logic as event tracking — see
  app/utils/experiments.server.ts) and, for treatment visitors only, fetches
  the day's Thompson Sampling ranking from /apps/pd/rank and reorders the
  collection grid client-side (daily cached draw — it does NOT change the
  collection's saved default order; control visitors are untouched).

  Everything stays easy to revert: delete this extension (or disable the
  "PD treatment (Thompson)" app embed in the theme editor) and every
  visitor sees the merchant's default order again.

  NOTE: the merchant must enable this block once via Theme editor →
  App embeds → "PD treatment (Thompson)". Until then the script is not
  loaded and all visitors see the default order.
{%- endcomment -%}

<script src="{{ 'pd-treatment.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "PD treatment (Thompson)",
  "target": "body",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}